## Control {{controlId}}: Limit physical access to organizational information systems, equipment, and the respective operating environments to authorized individuals.

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

{{#if tenantName}}
{{tenantName}} limits physical access to information systems and equipment to authorized individuals. The {{primaryDomain}} CUI environment is hosted in {{#if cloudEnvironment}}{{cloudEnvironment}}{{else}}cloud{{/if}} data centers managed by Microsoft, which maintain FedRAMP High authorization and physical security controls including biometric access, 24/7 surveillance, and mantrap entry points.
{{/if}}

{{#if approvedIpRange}}
Network access is restricted to the approved IP range ({{approvedIpRange}}), providing an additional layer of logical access control that complements physical security measures.
{{/if}}

{{#if wifiSsid}}
{{#if (eq wifiSsid "no-wifi")}}
Wireless network access is prohibited in areas where CUI is processed or stored, eliminating wireless attack vectors against physical access controls.
{{else}}
Wireless access is limited to the authorized SSID ({{wifiSsid}}) with enterprise-grade authentication and encryption.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

